<h2>The short version</h2>
<p>
  We collect the minimum needed to sell and support our plugins: your email when you ask us for
  something (such as a free trial download), your order and licence details, and anonymous, cookieless
  analytics. If you click <em>Accept All</em> on our cookie banner, we also use Google and Meta advertising
  tags to measure which of our ads bring visitors and sales; if you decline, they don&rsquo;t load. We
  don&rsquo;t sell your data, and you can have it deleted any time by emailing
  <a href="mailto:support@revaudio.net">support@revaudio.net</a>. The rest of this is the detail.
</p>

<h2>1. Who we are</h2>
<p>
  RevAudio (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;) builds and sells audio software plugins through this
  website, revaudio.net. We are the data controller for the personal data described here, and we are based at
  Yehudit Boulevard 8, Tel Aviv 67016, Israel. For any privacy question or request, contact
  <a href="mailto:info@revaudio.net">info@revaudio.net</a> or
  <a href="mailto:support@revaudio.net">support@revaudio.net</a>.
</p>

<h2>2. What we collect</h2>
<p><strong>Information you give us.</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>Your email address</strong>, when you request a free trial download, join our list, sign up for
    the founding-tester beta, or contact us. A trial request also means we send you the download link and a
    few emails about the trial, which you can stop at any time.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>What you write in our contact or affiliate forms</strong>, such as your name, email, and message.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Beta-survey responses</strong>, if you choose to take part: your answers to the survey
    questions, submitted with your email.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Anything you send us by email</strong> (for example a support request), including the contents
    of that message.
  </li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Purchase information.</strong></p>
<p>
  Purchases are processed by our reseller and <strong>merchant of record</strong>, a third-party payment
  provider. When you buy, you provide your name, email, and billing details <em>to the merchant of
  record</em>; we never see or store your card number. The merchant of record shares order details with us
  (such as your email, the product, and billing country) so we can deliver your download, issue your licence,
  and provide support. Its handling of your data is governed by its own privacy policy, linked at checkout.
</p>
<p><strong>Licence information.</strong></p>
<p>
  To deliver and protect your purchase we generate a <strong>licence key</strong> tied to your email. When
  the plugin activates or periodically validates that key, limited technical data (such as your licence key
  and the fact of a validation request) is processed so we can confirm the licence is valid.
</p>
<p><strong>Information collected automatically.</strong></p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>Cookieless analytics.</strong> We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to understand aggregate site
    traffic (such as page views, referrer, and country). It does <em>not</em> use cookies, does not
    fingerprint you, and does not track you across other sites.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Advertising tags, only if you accept cookies.</strong> If you click <em>Accept All</em>, we load
    the Google Ads tag and the Meta Pixel. They set cookies and tell Google and Meta which of our pages you
    viewed and whether you requested a trial or made a purchase, so we can see which ads work. If you arrived
    from a Google ad, we attach that ad click&rsquo;s identifier to your order so Google can count the sale,
    and at checkout the Google tag sends your email address in hashed (scrambled) form to match the sale to
    the ad. If you decline, none of these tags load and no ad-click identifier is attached to your order.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Sale reports to Meta, only if you accept cookies.</strong> If you accepted cookies before you
    buy, our server also reports the sale to Meta: the order value, currency, product, order number, and
    your email address in hashed form. If you declined, or never chose, no sale report is sent to Meta.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Server and security logs.</strong> Our hosting and edge providers process standard technical
    data (such as IP address and browser type) to serve the site, keep it secure, and prevent abuse.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2 id="cookies">3. Cookies &amp; local storage</h2>
<p>
  We ask before setting any advertising cookie. Only if you click <em>Accept All</em> on our cookie banner do
  the Google Ads tag and the Meta Pixel load and set their cookies (see above). Until you choose, or if you
  decline, we tell Google that consent is denied and set no advertising cookies. You can change your choice
  at any time with the <em>Cookie settings</em> link at the bottom of every page; declining after accepting
  also removes those cookies from our site.
</p>
<p>
  Your cookie choice and your shopping cart are stored locally in your own browser (in
  <code>localStorage</code>); that information stays on your device and the cart is not sent to us until you
  check out. Our analytics is cookieless (see above). Product videos load from YouTube&rsquo;s
  privacy-enhanced mode (youtube-nocookie.com) only when you press play.
</p>

<h2>4. Why we use your data (and our legal bases)</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>To deliver your purchase</strong>: download, licence key, and order support (to perform our contract with you).</li>
  <li><strong>To send you the emails you asked for</strong>: list updates or beta communications (with your consent, which you can withdraw at any time).</li>
  <li><strong>To improve the product</strong>: understanding beta-survey feedback and aggregate, cookieless traffic (our legitimate interest in improving our software and site).</li>
  <li><strong>To measure our advertising</strong>: advertising cookies, tags, and sale reports to Google and Meta (only with your consent, which you can withdraw at any time).</li>
  <li><strong>To keep the service secure and lawful</strong>: preventing abuse and meeting tax and legal obligations (legitimate interest and legal obligation).</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Who we share it with</h2>
<p>
  We do <strong>not</strong> sell your personal data. We use a small number of trusted service providers
  who process data on our behalf:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Our merchant of record</strong> (and its payment partners): checkout, payments, tax, and order management.</li>
  <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>: DNS and edge delivery, cookieless web analytics, and the workers that store beta-survey submissions, handle trial requests, and manage licences.</li>
  <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong>: hosting for this website.</li>
  <li><strong>Resend</strong>: sending our emails (download links, licence keys, trial and support emails).</li>
  <li><strong>Formspree</strong>: receiving messages from our contact and affiliate forms.</li>
  <li><strong>Google (Google Ads)</strong> and <strong>Meta</strong>: advertising measurement, as described in section 2, only with your consent. Their use of the data is also covered by their own privacy policies.</li>
  <li><strong>Google Maps</strong>: the embedded map on our About and Contact pages loads from Google and is covered by Google&rsquo;s privacy policy.</li>
  <li><strong>YouTube</strong>: product videos, loaded only when you press play.</li>
</ul>
<p>
  We may also disclose data if required by law, or to protect our rights, safety, or property.
</p>

<h2>6. International transfers</h2>
<p>
  We operate from Israel and our service providers may process data in other countries, including the
  United States. Where data is transferred internationally, we rely on the providers&rsquo; appropriate
  safeguards (such as standard contractual clauses or an applicable adequacy decision) to protect it.
</p>

<h2>7. How long we keep it</h2>
<p>
  We keep order and licence data for as long as your licence is active and as needed for support, tax, and
  legal record-keeping. We keep list and beta-signup emails until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete them.
  Beta-survey responses are kept for the duration of the beta programme and while we act on the feedback.
</p>

<h2>8. Your rights</h2>
<p>
  Depending on where you live, you have rights over your personal data, including the right to
  access it, correct it, delete it, restrict or object to its use, and receive a copy in a portable form.
  Where we rely on consent, you can withdraw it at any time. We do not sell personal data, and we do not
  discriminate against you for exercising your rights. To make a request, email
  <a href="mailto:support@revaudio.net">support@revaudio.net</a>, and we&rsquo;ll respond within the time
  your law requires. If you&rsquo;re in the EU/EEA or UK and unhappy with our response, you may complain to
  your local data-protection authority.
</p>

<h2>9. Security</h2>
<p>
  We use reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect your data, and we work with providers
  who maintain their own security and PCI compliance. No method of transmission or storage is perfectly
  secure, but we take protecting your data seriously and act promptly if something goes wrong.
</p>

<h2>10. Children</h2>
<p>
  Our products and site are intended for adults and are not directed at children. We do not knowingly
  collect personal data from children. If you believe a child has provided us data, contact us and we will
  delete it.
</p>

<h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>
  We may update this policy as our product line and the law evolve. Material changes will be dated at the
  top of this page.
</p>

<h2>12. Contact</h2>
<p>
  Privacy questions and requests: <a href="mailto:info@revaudio.net">info@revaudio.net</a><br />
  Support: <a href="mailto:support@revaudio.net">support@revaudio.net</a>
</p>
